find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{3}-9{t}^{2}-36t+2) \\\\  & =18{t}^{2}-18t-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18{t}^{2}-18t-36 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-t-2 & =0 \\\\ (t+1)(t-2) & =0 \\\\ t & =-1,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\ge 0,$ we disregard the negative solution. \n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude at $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033858/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5b347a0a7cb7316b86fb9aea2ef3ba0c1de22fae6af8da10da4fb28f670827b"} {"question" "q-138912" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f7ad419d93ee9149ffc25caab33e9435e5bfce01f2e6915a31407868c03eb4de"} {"question" "q-138912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033858/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5b347a0a7cb7316b86fb9aea2ef3ba0c1de22fae6af8da10da4fb28f670827b"} {"question" "q-138912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "t=10\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "t=2\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "t=3\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "t=6\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "t=8\\,\\text{s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033858/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5b347a0a7cb7316b86fb9aea2ef3ba0c1de22fae6af8da10da4fb